<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_channels",
    "When set, only channel members can send messages to the channel. Non-members attempting to send will receive an error. Service messages (NickServ, ChanServ) are not affected."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_lightbulb}>{dgettext("help_channels", "When to use it")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_channels",
    "The mode comes from classic IRC, where people outside a channel could send text into it. Set it when you want the channel modes to state clearly that only members may speak."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_terminal}>{dgettext("help_channels", "Usage")}</.help_h4>
<pre>/mode +n  {dgettext("help_channels", "Enable no external messages")}
/mode -n  {dgettext("help_channels", "Disable no external messages")}</pre>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_channels",
    "The command changes the channel you are looking at. You do not type the channel name."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_lightbulb}>{dgettext("help_channels", "How it works")}</.help_h4>
<ul>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_channels",
      "Even without this mode, a person must be in the channel to send messages to it. Someone who is not a member is always refused."
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_channels",
      "With the mode set, the refusal says that the channel does not accept external messages."
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_channels",
      "Members are not affected. To limit what members can say, use moderated mode instead."
    )}
  </li>
</ul>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_rules}>{dgettext("help_channels", "Rules and limits")}</.help_h4>
<ul>
  <li>
    {dgettext("help_channels", "Only channel operators and owners can set or remove this mode.")}
  </li>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_channels",
      "A new channel starts without this mode. In a registered channel the mode is saved and comes back after a restart."
    )}
  </li>
</ul>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_link}>{dgettext("help_channels", "See Also")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  <.help_link topic="mode-m">{dgettext("help_channels", "Moderated (+m)")}</.help_link>
  · <.help_link topic="cmd-mode">{dgettext("help_channels", "/mode")}</.help_link>
  ·
  <.help_link topic="channel-modes-overview">
    {dgettext("help_channels", "Channel Modes Overview")}
  </.help_link>
</p>
